            "content": "### What changed\n\n`GZipMiddleware` now accepts and forwards a `thread_minimum_size` setting:\n\n- `GZipMiddleware.__init__` defines it with a default of `128 * 1024`.\n- When gzip is negotiated, it constructs `GZipResponder` with:\n  ```python\n  thread_minimum_size=self.thread_minimum_size\n  ```\n\nHowever, `GZipResponder` changed to require that argument:\n\n```python\ndef __init__(\n    self,\n    app: ASGIApp,\n    minimum_size: int,\n    compresslevel: int = 9,\n    *,\n    thread_minimum_size: int,\n) -> None:\n```\n\nThat is compatible with the built-in middleware, which always passes the keyword, but it is not compatible with subclasses using the previous constructor pattern:\n\n```python\nsuper().__init__(app, minimum_size)\n```\n\nThe current gzip tests cover the new worker-thread behavior through `GZipMiddleware`, including custom thresholds, but none instantiate `GZipResponder` directly or exercise a legacy subclass constructor.\n\n### Focused backwards-compatible fix\n\nGive `GZipResponder.thread_minimum_size` the same default as the middleware:\n\n```python\nthread_minimum_size: int = 128 * 1024\n```\n\nKeep it keyword-only. This preserves:\n\n- Existing two-argument subclass calls.\n- Existing calls that provide `compresslevel`.\n- The current middleware behavior, since explicitly supplied values still win.\n- The new worker-thread compression feature.\n\nThe middleware\u2019s existing default and the responder\u2019s default should remain identical. If desired, a shared module-level constant could prevent the two defaults from drifting, but that is optional and not required for the compatibility fix.\n\n### Regression coverage\n\nAdd a focused constructor regression test in `tests/middleware/test_gzip.py`:\n\n1. Import `GZipResponder`.\n2. Define a small subclass whose constructor calls:\n   ```python\n   super().__init__(app, minimum_size)\n   ```\n3. Instantiate it with the legacy two-argument pattern.\n4. Assert construction succeeds, and optionally verify:\n   ```python\n   responder.thread_minimum_size == 128 * 1024\n   ```\n\nThat test directly reproduces the reported failure and ensures the default is actually installed.\n\nKeep the existing tests for:\n\n- `thread_minimum_size` configured through `GZipMiddleware`.\n- Non-streaming compression in a worker thread.\n- Streaming compression in a worker thread.\n\nTogether, those tests verify both compatibility for direct/custom responders and preservation of the new configured behavior.",
